    #    the bytes;
    #  - the budget figure, probe-emend-fullstyles-write-xml over probe-zip-xml,
    #    against the Milestone 2 ceiling of 458752 section bytes (decision 1, A),
    #    with the headroom or the excess in words and the file delta beside it;
    #  - the part's own cost, the new probe over probe-emend-sheets-write-xml,
    #    against the checkpoint of 25000 (a figure for the report, not a check:
    #    above it the maintainer re-rules before part 3's spec);
    #  - the whole growth since part 1's 375984, split into the part's own cost
    #    and the sheets probe's drift less probe-zip-xml's;
    #  - the dates feature's cost, outside the budget, as part 1's record carries
    #    it.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 2 P3 from M2 part 1 P5's size script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p1-p5/size.log; its change list is there), audited against
    # specs/0001 "Rules for every phase" and specs/0017, and grepped for part 1
    # P5's names, paths, subjects and typed lists. What differs, and why:
    #  A. The phase, the log directory, the record names and planning's files are
    #     part 2 P3's; the previous record and log are part 1 P5's, its commit
    #     read from the record. Part 6's record and part 1 P4's are no longer
    #     read: the growth is stated since part 1's record, as "Size" asks.
    #  B. The fourteenth probe, probe-emend-fullstyles-write-xml, is built,
    #     measured and run on the generated package; it has no earlier figure and
    #     is listed as new beside the thirteen classified.
    #  C. The figures block is rebuilt for "Size": the ceiling is 458752, the
    #     part's own cost is over the sheets probe and is printed against the
    #     25000 checkpoint, the growth since 375984 is split into the part's cost
    #     and the drift. Part 1 P5's acceptance checks (the sheets probe 100000
    #     below P4's) go with that phase.
    #  D. The generated packages run the new probe too, on the two-sheet
    #     package with a font name, and its second output's styles part is read
    #     back by ElementTree: the three collections grown by one each, the new
    #     cell format's ids, apply flags and two children, and the number cell's
    #     style.
    #  E. P1 verification ruling 7: this script's standard error goes to
    #     <scratch>/p3/out/size.stderr from its start and is counted in its last
    #     block, expecting 0, with a control on a copy one byte longer.
    #  F. The build directory is <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p2-p3-size; the
    #     run log reads the release binaries back from there by the hash lines.
    #  G. Attempt 2: attempt 1 printed <repo> and <home> with no root line for
    #     either (the scan's placeholder check, a structural failure; the gap
    #     part 1 P5's size log had, specs/0016 P5 verification ruling 3). The two
    #     root lines are added and nothing else changed.
    #
    # Usage: m2p2-p3-size.sh <phase commit> <record output file> > <scratch file>,
    # run from the repository root; the caller moves the output to
    # records/logs/m2p2-p3/size.log and the record to
    # records/size-m2p2-<utc-date>-<shortsha>.md.
